    {
      "role": "user",
      "content": "can u explain exactly what the seller is responsible for under CIF Incoterms 2020? we're looking at a shipment of circuit boards from seoul to hamburg so need to know the risk transfer point and what insurance they gotta cover.",
      "source": "evaluator"
    },
    {
      "role": "assistant",
      "content": "Under CIF Incoterms 2020, the seller is responsible for the cost of bringing the goods to the named port of destination in Hamburg. This includes contracting and paying for carriage (main transport) and insurance to cover the loss or damage of the goods during transit. Crucially, risk transfers from the seller to the buyer once the goods have been loaded onto the vessel in Seoul.",
      "source": "target",
