    {
      "role": "user",
      "content": "got it. so we just need to make sure we have those documents from them. one more thing, is there any specific type of insurance they are required to get under CIF 2020? i think i heard something about it being \"minimum cover\" but i want to be sure so we aren't left hanging if something goes wrong.",
      "source": "evaluator"
    },
    {
      "role": "assistant",
      "content": "Yes, CIF mandates that the seller purchases insurance covering at least the minimum required coverage, which is typically \"Institute Cargo Clauses (C).\" This minimum coverage protects against specified perils like loss or damage to the goods during transit. While this cover is often the baseline, you should always negotiate for broader coverage, such as Institute Cargo Clauses (A), for maximum protection.",
      "source": "target",
